author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 420
acceptance_criteria: "A serve entry records a bounded number of candidate rows independent of open item count, and the bound is declared in the contract rather than implied by a surface; Retention and compaction are expressed in the same unit, so the trigger threshold is reachable by the policy that follows it and the ledger has a declared steady-state ceiling in bytes; The read path does not rewrite the whole ledger on every serve, proved by measuring bytes written per read at three corpus sizes including the million-item tier; Ledger writes are measured under a concurrent fleet at the scale target and the published numbers state reads per second per workspace and the observed lock wait distribution; A negative control proves the declared ceiling gate fails when a surface reintroduces one row per open item"
parent: pm-9rxu
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: Bound persisted context samples and append work with byte-based compaction and measured receipts
expected_result: Persist at most 256 serving rows and 262144 bytes without rewriting each serve
actual_result: At 10000/100000/1000000 rows mean written bytes remain about 18KB and each tier compacts 2 of 40 serves; physical ledgers remain below 238KB; throughput and min/p50/p95/max lock waits are published
